## Decision
Issue three independent pairwise verdicts. For each pair pick the translation
that is overall better — considering adequacy, fluency, coherence, and style
match. If a pair is genuinely indistinguishable, output "tie", but prefer a
clear pick when there's any meaningful difference.

Be transitive when honest — but if your evidence supports a non-transitive
ordering (rare) report what you actually see; do not force a global order.

## Output schema
{
  "a_vs_b": "A" | "B" | "tie",
  "a_vs_c": "A" | "C" | "tie",
  "b_vs_c": "B" | "C" | "tie",
  "rationale": "<= 60 words summarizing the relative strengths"
}

Rules:
- Output JSON only. No markdown fences, no prose outside the JSON.
- The rationale should reference A / B / C only, never the underlying
  system identities.
- Ties should be the exception; reserve them for genuinely
  indistinguishable pairs.
- Each ``*_vs_*`` field must use only the two letters in its name plus
  "tie" — e.g. ``a_vs_b`` is never "C".
